# Course assignment briefs (local only).
Assignment/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files too large to push to GitHub.
#
# GitHub warns above 50 MB and refuses anything over 100 MB in a single push.
# Only the two files that cross those lines are listed here; every other data
# file, and the trained model, are small enough to stay tracked so the
# repository is self-contained.
#
# Both files below are rebuilt from the raw downloads by:
#   python spam_malware_detection_model/build_datasets.py
#   python spam_malware_detection_model/spam/clean_spam_dataset.py
# and both are published on Hugging Face, so nothing is lost by leaving them
# out of git. See the links in README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 240 MB. Over the 100 MB hard limit. Intermediate file: only
# spam/clean_spam_dataset.py reads it, on the way to the file below.
dataset/spam_train_dataset.csv

# ~101 MB. Under the hard limit but well over the 50 MB warning, so every clone
# would carry it. This is the file the spam model trains on, and it is on
# Hugging Face.
dataset/spam_train_clean.csv

# The 87 MB embedded-firmware image table exceeds GitHub's 50 MB warning.
# It is reproducible from the Kaggle command in dataset/datamunge/INFO.md.
dataset/datamunge/firmware/firmware.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Malware platform expansion: raw Kaggle downloads and the normalized training
# tables built from them. These total ~560 MB and some Kaggle licences do not
# allow redistributing the source files on a public repository.
#
# Every folder's INFO.md records the exact `kaggle datasets download -d <ref>`
# command, and `python spam_malware_detection_model/build_datasets.py` rebuilds
# every normalized CSV below. That keeps the repository small and reproducible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dataset/**/*.csv
dataset/*.csv
dataset/**/*.ipynb
dataset/fanbyprinciple/
dataset/datamunge/imagery/
# Keep provenance notes: only the bulk payload files are ignored.
!dataset/**/INFO.md
!dataset/joebeachcapital/malware_android_tuandromd.csv

# Python environment and build artifacts
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Local secrets: copy .env.example to .env and never commit the copy.
.env

# Local scratch files from debugging and review sessions.
innovation-g2/_debug_*.py
innovation-g2/_review_*.py
render/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.zcodeignore
*.log
